<title>INDIA: Indian forex market shut for national holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian forex market shut for national holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian foreign exchange market was shut on Monday as banks across the country closed for a national holiday.</p>
<p>The market reopens on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Indian rupee ended Friday steady at 35.84/85 per dollar. -- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
